compliments or ten thousand ovations.

15:44.580 --> 15:46.500
Only the poet understood...

15:47.500 --> 15:53.720
She wanted to push herself further
and further, pass her own limits.

15:53.720 --> 16:01.520
He understood because he, too, was a creator,
and had often encountered those limits.

16:02.640 --> 16:04.650
So the poet began to sing...

16:05.400 --> 16:07.020
for the songstress.

16:11.700 --> 16:13.780
It was the song of the chrysalis.

16:14.320 --> 16:15.530
The chrysalis?

16:15.990 --> 16:20.410
This chrysalis was more beautiful than
any gem in the entire world.

16:20.410 --> 16:22.660
Any who saw it, praised it.

16:22.660 --> 16:27.460
But hidden within, there was an
even more beautiful truth.

16:27.460 --> 16:29.050
Truth?

16:29.710 --> 16:32.760
<i>Wings slumber inside you.</i>

16:36.180 --> 16:39.510
A burst of lightning coursed through
the songstress's body.

16:42.100 --> 16:46.230
<i>Will you stay in that hard,
cramped shell forever?</i>

16:46.230 --> 16:48.730
<i>Is that what you truly desire?</i>

16:48.730 --> 16:50.190
<i>It is not.</i>

16:50.530 --> 16:56.030
The poet's song was like a spider's thread,
